      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::cli-read-no-encoding",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Questions file read lacks explicit encoding",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "lev/cli.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "cli.py line 24: Path(args.questions).read_text() with no encoding argument - a non-UTF8 file raises UnicodeDecodeError, which is not in the caught tuple (only ValueError, KeyError, OSError) so it surfaces as a raw traceback instead of a clean CLI error"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pass encoding=\"utf-8\" to read_text() and include UnicodeDecodeError (or UnicodeError) in the except tuple so bad-encodings get the same clean 'lev: error:' treatment.",
